{# The `system` stanza. Rendered since the push became a full `load override`:
   the device's whole configuration is replaced by this artifact, so anything
   not in it is deleted -- and `system` is where the management path lives.

   WHAT IS DATA AND WHAT IS NOT, and why:

   * `host-name` is the firewall's NAME in Infrahub, the one value here the
     model genuinely owns.
   * `services` and `management-instance` are the DELIVERY PATH, not intent.
     The reconciler arrives over SSH (and vrnetlab forwards NETCONF on 830) to
     fxp0 inside `mgmt_junos`; every value but this one makes the firewall
     unreachable, so modelling them would add nothing but a way to break the
     push. `assert_junos_lifeline` refuses an artifact that lacks them.
   * The two `encrypted-password` values are the LAB'S EXISTING HASHES, copied
     verbatim from lab/configs/fw/vsrx/junos.conf (SHA-512 of the password
     vrnetlab and containerlab already use; that file says how it was made).
     They live in this template, never in the graph: a credential in the model
     reaches every branch, every export, the GraphQL API and the MCP server's
     read access, while here it is where it already was -- in git, and in the
     artifact the device must receive. Never a `plain-text-password-value`:
     vrnetlab's init.conf writes one, the device keeps it verbatim as
     cleartext, and a full override is what finally removes it.
   * `root-login allow` is vrnetlab's own setting, kept so that the replace
     removes nothing the device was booted with.

   Nothing else is rendered because nothing else runs: neither junos.conf nor
   the running device has syslog, NTP or a name server. Adding them here would
   be inventing configuration. #}
system {
    host-name {{ node }};
    root-authentication {
        encrypted-password "$6$otternetlab$1ni88meu2WmQvWmveReLJXVojb6LSSOmcM75qXpzCLKzUzoU63yFywA2YQLoFI2QDjo4RXF28DbWY9wg9gKT71";
    }
    login {
        user admin {
            class super-user;
            authentication {
                encrypted-password "$6$otternetlab$1ni88meu2WmQvWmveReLJXVojb6LSSOmcM75qXpzCLKzUzoU63yFywA2YQLoFI2QDjo4RXF28DbWY9wg9gKT71";
            }
        }
    }
    services {
        ssh {
            root-login allow;
        }
        netconf {
            ssh;
        }
    }
    management-instance;
}
